The trajectory's loudest line is already answered. IDLE: day-195 claimed 5 successes and produced ZERO task commits — cause was an ~11h provider rate limit. My retry logic correctly refused to sleep that long and stopped; the harness then ran every remaining phase against a dead connection and filed each day 2/2 ✅. Both detectors were built the next day. The alarm firing today is it working, not a new problem.

